This uses four NEON accumulators with fused multiply-add, processing 16 floats per iteration. Splitting the sum across independent accumulators keeps rounding error well inside the stated tolerance for inputs in [-1, 1]. The loop is bound by memory bandwidth at n = 16M, so the vector code should be close to the best achievable. I have not compiled or run it.

