This is a double-precision NEON kernel. It processes 8 pixels per group as four `float64x2_t` vectors, which gives the core several independent dependency chains. A group stops as soon as all its lanes have escaped. Dummy lanes in the partial last group are set to escape on the first iteration. I did not compile or run it.

