This is a NEON version that processes 8 pixels per group, using four independent float64 vectors so the FMA dependency chains overlap. It skips pixels inside the main cardioid and the period-2 bulb, since they never escape. Each group stops as soon as every lane has escaped. I haven't compiled or run it.

